-- Transcription of layout-language-consult.md §5.5 (lines 588-599),
-- clean-room LengYue, portrait class. Disclosed adjustments beyond the
-- ones already covered in lengyue_landscape.lyt's header comment:
--   - `A_top[*, action]` uses '*' as a domain wildcard (the document's own
--     comment reads "A_go (+) A_common on one reserved strip", i.e. this
--     leaf merges two census domains into one strip). LYT's Domain type
--     has no wildcard/union member; we pick 'common' as the representative
--     domain, consistent with §4.3's own position that domain tagging is
--     advisory, not load-bearing for geometry.
--   - `I_engine[...]{28px, envelope as above}`: "as above" is prose
--     referencing §5.4's envelope states; spelled out explicitly here
--     rather than parsed literally (no such backreference exists in the
--     grammar).
--   - `T( tree, CP-* )[BLACK BOX]{pref 1fr, min 200px}` abbreviates the
--     black box further than §5.4 (bare `tree` with no bracket, and a
--     `CP-*` wildcard standing in for all five tabs). Expanded here to the
--     same six children as the landscape encoding — the census entities
--     are the same, only the prose shorthand differs — with each child's
--     own min set to 200px so the T node's structurally-derived min
--     (componentwise max of children, §4.1 line 298-302) reproduces the
--     document's explicit `min 200px` for the whole group.
--   - AMENDMENT 3 (ledger row 1715, gap-amendment-build): the root V(...)
--     gets `gap 12px`, `--space-medium` (`frontend/src/assets/css/
--     theme.css`'s own words: "section-level gap, content-block
--     separation"). Landscape's OUTER split uses the wider `--space-loose`
--     tier (20px) for its board-vs-side-column split, a clean two-way
--     major-region seam with generous width to spare; portrait's root
--     stacks bands in a narrower viewport, so the next tier down is the
--     disclosed, deliberate choice here, not an infeasibility workaround
--     (this class stayed OPTIMAL at `--space-loose` too when probed — see
--     build report). The new tree/panels/preview row below gets its own
--     `gap 4px` (`--space-tight`), matching landscape's identical row.
--
--   - TREE ALWAYS VISIBLE / boardRail / previewBoard (ledger row ~1735):
--     same three commissioner-driven changes as lengyue_landscape.lyt —
--     read that file's header in full for the shared rationale
--     (grounding citations, presence-menu mechanism disclosure, the
--     aspect-leaf generalization, the boardRail-as-popover open fork).
--     This file's own class-specific choices, not covered there:
--       - boardRail: the as-is app's 168px reservation is a WIDTH (a
--         left-edge rail column); portrait's root V partitions on
--         HEIGHT, so there is no literal "left edge" in a single-column
--         stack. Reinterpreted as a 168px-tall HORIZONTAL strip at the
--         TOP of the page (root V's new first child, before A_top) —
--         "top" being the portrait analog of "leftmost/first" in the
--         root's own child ORDER (matching the ruling's own "left edge
--         as today is the conservative choice": same numeric value,
--         same leading structural position, axis reinterpreted the way
--         every other shared-identity leaf in this pair of files already
--         is between classes). No stronger portrait-specific precedent
--         exists to ground a different number against — flagged as a
--         judgment call, not a re-derivation.
--       - previewBoard: reservation scaled DOWN from landscape's 160px to
--         96px (`min=pref=max=96px, aspect 1`) — "modest... scaled
--         sensibly to the region" (the ruling's own phrasing). Portrait's
--         tree/panels/preview row shares its width budget with the
--         tree's fixed 140px and the T node's 200px floor inside the
--         FULL VIEWPORT WIDTH (no elastic side-column buffer the way
--         landscape has); 96px is the down-scaled choice that keeps this
--         row's fixed+floor total (140+96+200=436px plus two 4px gaps)
--         comfortably under every representative portrait width this
--         prototype's own OVERLAY_SIZES table tests at 768px and up,
--         while genuinely tightening the narrowest two probes (540x960,
--         420x880) — see the build report's before/after feasibility
--         table for the measured outcome at each size, disclosed rather
--         than silently absorbed either way.
--
--   - AMENDMENT 4 (ledger row 1737, per-valuation presence solving,
--     SPEC-AMENDMENTS.md): boardRail and previewBoard below are now
--     genuinely `@toggle(user, release)` in this file's own concrete
--     syntax, same as lengyue_landscape.lyt — see that file's own
--     boardRail header note for the full rationale (the DEFAULT-OFF
--     state itself still lives at the registration layer, `runner.py`'s
--     `Registration.default_valuation`, not in this file's text).
--
--   - LYT TOOLBAR ONTOLOGY REENCODE (commissioner-ratified 2026-08-11,
--     ledger rows 1930/1931; `.claude/dispatch-reports/
--     lyt-toolbar-ontology-reencode.md`) — the commission's four points,
--     applied to THIS class: `A_top` is RENAMED `A_app[common, action]`
--     (same tree position, root child '1' — the widget id changes, the
--     structure doesn't) and `I_engine` is RENAMED `A_engine[go,
--     action+info]` (same tree position, root child '3'), now genuinely
--     `envelope: {disconnected, connected}` and MOUNTED for the first
--     time — portrait's own `I_engine` leaf previously mounted NOTHING
--     (disclosed W3 narrowing, `lyt-widget-registry.ts`'s prior
--     "class-scoped overrides" note: portrait's tree structurally
--     separated `I_engine` from `A_top`, so landscape's merged-Toolbar
--     disposition never carried over here). This reencode closes that
--     gap: portrait now has a REAL, working engine cluster it never had
--     before, not merely a rename. No path shift anywhere in this file
--     (unlike landscape, whose side column genuinely lost a V-child) —
--     portrait's own root V already kept `A_top`/`I_engine` as two
--     SEPARATE, non-adjacent children (the board composite sits between
--     them), so collapsing three leaves into two never applied here to
--     begin with. Reservations: `160px` (A_app) / `60px` (A_engine,
--     envelope-reserved) are a REAL Playwright measurement of the
--     realized components at portrait's own pinned representative
--     widths (420px — `tests/test_lyt.py`'s own
--     `test_lengyue_portrait_default_valuation_solves_optimal_at_420x880`;
--     1080px — `runner.py`'s own SCREEN_SIZES portrait point), taking
--     the worse (narrower, 420px) case per component plus a ~10px
--     margin — see the dispatch report's measurement table. Was `28px`
--     each (bare fixed shorthand) pre-reencode, a reservation this
--     encoding's own real content never actually fit inside even before
--     today (portrait's engine strip mounted nothing at all, and the
--     app strip's own real content already needed to wrap well past one
--     28px row) — this is a genuine, disclosed CORRECTION of an
--     under-measured prior value, not merely a resize for the new split.
--   - OPTION C TAB-SKELETON ENCODING (2026-08-11, ledger row 1937's
--     ratified consult; work item lyt-tab-skeleton-encoding). Same
--     re-homing + one-level-open shape as `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s own
--     header note (read in full there for the grounding citations,
--     the settings-pane conservative-superset disclosure, the per-panel
--     height groundings/estimates, the CP-other L5c restructure, and the
--     BOTH-AXES TENSION note) — this class differs only in its
--     per-child `min` (200px, matching this file's own pre-existing
--     WRAPPER_MIN-analog convention, vs. landscape's 160px) for the two
--     still-opaque CP-library/CP-cards leaves; every genuinely NEW number
--     (the 838/664/204px composite floors, the per-panel floors) is
--     IDENTICAL across both classes — the underlying components render
--     the same regardless of screen orientation, so there is no honest
--     portrait-specific number to derive differently. Portrait's own
--     narrower available width makes the 838px settings floor and the
--     664px analysis floor considerably more likely to be the binding
--     constraint here than in landscape — reported, not pre-empted, in
--     the delivery report's solver results.
--
--     REPAIR (2026-08-11, `.claude/dispatch-reports/lyt-optionc-review.md`
--     Findings 2/3, corrected in `.claude/dispatch-reports/lyt-optionc-
--     repair.md`): same fixes as `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s own header note
--     (read there for the full derivation) — the T(...)'s own wrapping
--     slot now carries an explicit `min 200px` (this file's own
--     pre-existing per-child marker reservation), so the emitter's
--     collapsed blackbox leaf reads that declared min directly instead of
--     re-deriving the solver's own componentwise-max floor from the (now
--     much deeper) composite children; and the settings-substrip demand
--     is corrected from the delivered wave's inflated 97ch/880px to the
--     actual 92ch/838px (a systematic +1-per-label ch-count error, five of
--     six labels affected — see the landscape header's Finding 3 note for
--     the full per-label table).
--
--     FLOW-CAPABLE SETTINGS SUBSTRIP (2026-08-11, work item
--     lyt-settings-live-opening, ledger rows 2007/2009): identical
--     derivation to `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s own header note (read there
--     in full — the six item widths, `research/lyt/flow.py`'s
--     `narrowest_width_for_row_count`/`flow_envelope`, the 2-row/443px/
--     60px design point, the BOTH-AXES-TENSION-driven composite min drop
--     from 838px to 443px). Applied identically here per this file's own
--     established convention (this section's own header line 120-121:
--     "every genuinely NEW number ... is IDENTICAL across both classes —
--     the underlying components render the same regardless of screen
--     orientation, so there is no honest portrait-specific number to
--     derive differently"). Portrait's own narrower available width
--     (line 122-126 above) means this correction is, if anything, MORE
--     load-bearing here than in landscape.
--
--     REPAIR (2026-08-12, independent review Finding 3 — identical
--     correction to `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s own REPAIR header note,
--     read there in full): `settingsSubstrip` moves `{60px}` -> `{77px}`
--     (the review's own live-measured 67px + this file's established
--     ~10px margin posture). Composite `min` unchanged at 443px (the new
--     281px height floor stays under the 443px width floor).
layout lengyue-portrait =
  {min 0px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 12px} V(
    @toggle(user, release) {min 168px, pref 168px, max 168px} boardRail[common, info+action],
    {160px} A_app[common, action],
    {pref 1fr} V(
      {width 100fr, aspect 1} B[board],
      {24px} I_board[board, info],
      {28px} A_board[board, action]
    ),
    {60px, envelope: {disconnected, connected}} A_engine[go, action+info],
    {pref 1fr, gap 4px} H(
      {min 140px, pref 140px, max 140px} tree[board, info+action],
      {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf} T(
        {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content unbounded, scroll v} CP-library[common],
        {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content unbounded, scroll v} CP-cards[common],
        {min 443px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 4px} V(
          {77px, boundary, content bounded} settingsSubstrip[common],
          {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content unbounded, scroll v} settingsPane[common]
        ),
        {min 664px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 4px} V(
          {min 80px, pref 80px, max 80px, boundary, content designed} timelineStrip[go],
          {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf} T(
            {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 4px} V(
              {min 90px, pref 90px, max 90px, boundary, content designed} AT_basic_interval[go],
              {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_basic_scoreLead[go],
              {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_basic_mergedDelta[go]
            ),
            {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 4px} V(
              {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_dist_deltaDist[go],
              {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_dist_mistakeGap[go]
            ),
            {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 4px} V(
              {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_stab_stability[go],
              {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_stab_crossCorr[go]
            ),
            {min 580px, pref 580px, max inf, boundary, content designed} AT_multires[go]
          )[ANALYSIS TABS]
        ),
        {min 204px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 4px} V(
          -- REPAIR (2026-08-11, `.claude/dispatch-reports/
          -- lyt-realization-wave-review.md` Finding 1): 40px -> 264px,
          -- same corrected measured reservation as `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s
          -- own `otherColorDebug` (that file's header carries the full
          -- measurement derivation: own Playwright rig, 1920x1080/1280x1024/
          -- 1080x1920-portrait-class, max 254px at 1280x1024 + ~10px margin).
          -- Not independently re-measured against PORTRAIT's own real
          -- operating column width specifically (this class's own T-node
          -- wraps at 200px min, narrower than landscape's 160px, but this
          -- class's checked 1080x1920 representative point measured a WIDER
          -- 931px operating column there, giving 232px -- under the
          -- landscape-derived 264px) -- using landscape's larger, measured
          -- number here is the conservative, disclosed choice, not a
          -- from-scratch portrait measurement.
          {min 264px, pref 264px, max 264px, boundary, content designed} otherColorDebug[debug],
          {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content unbounded, scroll v} otherBand[common]
        )
      )[BLACK BOX],
      @toggle(user, release) {min 96px, pref 96px, max 96px, aspect 1} previewBoard[common, info]
    )
  )
